'' NAME renames through the runtime's fb_hPathRename (UTF-16 on Windows, libc's rename elsewhere); LOCK and UNLOCK take a range whose second bound is 0
'' when no 'to' was written.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/file-name-lock.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered

'' The runtime's path helper (lib/rt/src/fs/upath.tiko), not libc's rename as fbc emits: the
'' names are UTF-16 on Windows, UTF-8 if valid, else the ANSI code page.
'' EXPECT-OUT: declare i32 fb_hPathRename(ptr $0, ptr $1)
'' EXPECT-NOT: fb_Rename
'' EXPECT-NOT: fb_FileName

'' The 'Large' spelling, and i64 bounds whatever the source types were.
'' EXPECT-OUT: declare i32 fb_FileLockLarge(i32 $0, i64 $1, i64 $2)
'' EXPECT-OUT: declare i32 fb_FileUnlockLarge(i32 $0, i64 $1, i64 $2)

'' The GOLDEN is what pins the ARGUMENTS -- that 'lock #1, 5' passes a second bound
'' of 0 and 'lock #1, 3 to 9' passes 9. A substring cannot say which call got which.
'' GOLDEN: expected/file-name-lock.out
